    "most_fragile_aspect": "The trend is not fragile in sign: all 11 variants stay positive, and only two lose significance. The single weakest aspect is the thin, family-concentrated all-18-stage panel (variant g): only 14 units from 11 families cover all 18 stages, and its slope drops to 0.0258 (r 0.404, unit t-test p = 0.117) with a family-clustered 95% CI [-0.0045, 0.0624] that includes 0. That is a composition effect, not a contradiction: removing the single largest g family (interaction_0231, 54/252 records) restores the slope to 0.0445, and the broader panel of 381 units with >= 6 stages gives the strongest slope of all (0.0624). Second weakest is the non-floor-p subset (variant i, slope 0.01058), significant but roughly a quarter of the primary magnitude, so the floor-p tier carries most of the signal. The variants that reweight (j, k) and the median (c) roughly halve the slope yet stay clearly positive with clustered CIs excluding zero."
